WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.764 --> 00:00:09.507
Nadia Pearce | Halyard Buyers Advocacy: —sorry, I just had to let the dog out, she was scratching at the door. Okay. Can you both hear me okay?

2
00:00:09.979 --> 00:00:11.390
Tash Kumar: Yep, all good.

3
00:00:11.789 --> 00:00:12.449
Rhys Gallagher: Yep.

4
00:00:13.472 --> 00:00:21.220
Nadia Pearce | Halyard Buyers Advocacy: Great. So I've hit record, that's just for my notes, is that okay? It gets deleted after we're done with it.

5
00:00:21.978 --> 00:00:23.373
Tash Kumar: Yeah, that's fine.

6
00:00:23.665 --> 00:00:28.512
Nadia Pearce | Halyard Buyers Advocacy: Lovely. And Dan's going to jump on a bit later, did he message you?

7
00:00:29.440 --> 00:00:36.920
Rhys Gallagher: Yeah, he said he's got a client till quarter past, so he'll join after that. He said just start without him.

8
00:00:39.734 --> 00:00:47.437
Nadia Pearce | Halyard Buyers Advocacy: Perfect. That actually works well, it gives me a chance to get to know you first. So how are you both?

9
00:00:47.437 --> 00:00:50.372
Nadia Pearce | Halyard Buyers Advocacy: Tash, have you just come off a shift?

10
00:00:51.339 --> 00:00:58.691
Tash Kumar: No, I'm on nights tomorrow. So today's my, um, my sleep normally day. I've had a coffee. I'm okay.

11
00:00:59.135 --> 00:01:02.157
Nadia Pearce | Halyard Buyers Advocacy: Oh, that's brutal. Where are you working?

12
00:01:02.650 --> 00:01:05.412
Tash Kumar: At the hospital at Chermside. In ICU.

13
00:01:05.688 --> 00:01:10.571
Nadia Pearce | Halyard Buyers Advocacy: Wow. Okay. Respect. And Rhys, you're a sparky, is that right? From the form?

14
00:01:10.920 --> 00:01:14.915
Rhys Gallagher: Yeah, electrician. I do mostly commercial. Fit outs and that.

15
00:01:15.211 --> 00:01:22.965
Nadia Pearce | Halyard Buyers Advocacy: Great. Okay, so, just quickly about me, I'm Nadia, I run Halyard, it's a small buyers agency, there's three of us.

16
00:01:22.965 --> 00:01:31.087
Nadia Pearce | Halyard Buyers Advocacy: I used to be a selling agent on the north side for about nine years, and I started doing this in 2019.

17
00:01:31.087 --> 00:01:37.363
Nadia Pearce | Halyard Buyers Advocacy: I'll tell you more about what we do later, but first I want to hear about you.

18
00:01:37.363 --> 00:01:40.686
Nadia Pearce | Halyard Buyers Advocacy: What's going on, what's got you thinking about buying?

19
00:01:41.459 --> 00:01:46.356
Tash Kumar: Um, so we're renting in Lutwitch, in a unit, we've been there three years.

20
00:01:46.356 --> 00:01:51.952
Tash Kumar: And we've been saving for ages, and we sort of, we just want to stop renting.

21
00:01:51.952 --> 00:01:57.898
Tash Kumar: Our rent's gone up like a hundred and twenty dollars a week in the last two years.

22
00:01:58.579 --> 00:01:59.825
Rhys Gallagher: Hundred and thirty.

23
00:02:00.460 --> 00:02:04.833
Tash Kumar: Hundred and thirty. And it's, like, we're paying someone else's mortgage, you know.

24
00:02:07.594 --> 00:02:12.009
Nadia Pearce | Halyard Buyers Advocacy: Yeah. I hear that every week. So this is your first place?

25
00:02:12.970 --> 00:02:14.402
Tash Kumar: First place, yeah.

26
00:02:16.273 --> 00:02:17.682
Rhys Gallagher: First home buyers.

27
00:02:18.302 --> 00:02:21.274
Nadia Pearce | Halyard Buyers Advocacy: Okay. Great. And have you been looking much?

28
00:02:22.225 --> 00:02:26.391
Tash Kumar: A bit. Mostly online. We've been to, like, five or six opens.

29
00:02:26.391 --> 00:02:31.946
Tash Kumar: We went to a townhouse in Kedron that we really liked but it went really quickly.

30
00:02:31.946 --> 00:02:36.113
Tash Kumar: Like, before we even had a chance to get our act together.

31
00:02:36.680 --> 00:02:39.357
Rhys Gallagher: It was gone in like four days.

32
00:02:39.755 --> 00:02:46.564
Nadia Pearce | Halyard Buyers Advocacy: Yeah, that happens a lot with townhouses at the moment, especially the ones in the first home buyer price range.

33
00:02:46.564 --> 00:02:50.990
Nadia Pearce | Halyard Buyers Advocacy: Everyone's chasing the same stuff. Do you know roughly what it went for?

34
00:02:51.739 --> 00:02:57.756
Rhys Gallagher: The agent said offers over eight-fifty, and then someone said it went for, um, nine-twenty? Something like that.

35
00:02:58.353 --> 00:03:03.805
Nadia Pearce | Halyard Buyers Advocacy: Yep. That sounds about right. Okay, so tell me, what are you thinking? Townhouse, unit, house?

36
00:03:04.655 --> 00:03:11.582
Tash Kumar: I mean, honestly, we'd love a house. But I don't think we can afford a house anywhere near here.

37
00:03:12.332 --> 00:03:20.520
Rhys Gallagher: We had a look at houses out in, like, Bracken Ridge, Zilmere, but Tash doesn't want to be too far from work.

38
00:03:20.986 --> 00:03:28.538
Tash Kumar: Because of nights. Like, when I finish a night shift at eight in the morning, I don't want to drive forty minutes.

39
00:03:28.538 --> 00:03:31.971
Tash Kumar: I just want to get home and go to bed.

40
00:03:32.372 --> 00:03:41.159
Nadia Pearce | Halyard Buyers Advocacy: Yeah, completely. That's actually a really important one, I'll write that down. So, distance to Chermside is a big priority for you.

41
00:03:42.027 --> 00:03:43.955
Tash Kumar: Yeah. Like twenty minutes max.

42
00:03:44.210 --> 00:03:46.772
Nadia Pearce | Halyard Buyers Advocacy: Okay. And Rhys, where's your work?

43
00:03:47.673 --> 00:03:54.686
Rhys Gallagher: All over. Wherever the job is. Mostly the city, Fortitude Valley, sometimes out at the airport. I drive.

44
00:03:55.560 --> 00:03:59.388
Nadia Pearce | Halyard Buyers Advocacy: Okay, so you're flexible. And you've got a work vehicle?

45
00:03:59.932 --> 00:04:05.315
Rhys Gallagher: Yeah, I've got the ute, it's mine, not the company's. And I've got all my tools.

46
00:04:05.315 --> 00:04:12.717
Rhys Gallagher: So I need, like, a lockable garage. I can't leave tools in the ute on the street. I've had them nicked before.

47
00:04:13.741 --> 00:04:18.351
Nadia Pearce | Halyard Buyers Advocacy: Oh no. Yeah. Okay, that's a must. Secure garage, lock up. And what else?

48
00:04:18.606 --> 00:04:22.035
Tash Kumar: Three bedrooms would be good. Or two and a study.

49
00:04:22.035 --> 00:04:27.864
Tash Kumar: We've got a cat, so, um, pet friendly, which I know with a body corporate can be—

50
00:04:27.940 --> 00:04:35.666
Nadia Pearce | Halyard Buyers Advocacy: Yep. That's one of the things I'd check in the by-laws. It's mostly fine now in Queensland, but it's worth checking.

51
00:04:36.312 --> 00:04:40.884
Tash Kumar: And some outdoor space. Even a courtyard. Just somewhere to sit outside.

52
00:04:41.297 --> 00:04:42.342
Rhys Gallagher: A barbecue.

53
00:04:42.696 --> 00:04:45.038
Tash Kumar: A barbecue. Ha. That's his must.

54
00:04:45.800 --> 00:04:52.095
Nadia Pearce | Halyard Buyers Advocacy: Ha. Everyone's got one. Okay so, can I ask about budget? What have you been thinking?

55
00:04:52.615 --> 00:04:58.921
Rhys Gallagher: That's kind of what we want to talk to Dan about. We've got, um, about $85,000 saved.

56
00:04:58.921 --> 00:05:03.002
Rhys Gallagher: And then we were looking at the five percent deposit thing.

57
00:05:05.592 --> 00:05:07.245
Tash Kumar: The first home guarantee.

58
00:05:08.075 --> 00:05:12.745
Nadia Pearce | Halyard Buyers Advocacy: Yep. That's one Dan will be able to explain better than me.

59
00:05:12.745 --> 00:05:17.415
Nadia Pearce | Halyard Buyers Advocacy: But okay, so you're looking at going in with a small deposit.

60
00:05:18.448 --> 00:05:23.128
Tash Kumar: Yeah. And we just, we don't really know what we can afford.

61
00:05:23.128 --> 00:05:30.148
Tash Kumar: Dan did a quick calculation and said maybe 900, 950, but he wanted to look at everything properly.

62
00:05:30.914 --> 00:05:38.966
Nadia Pearce | Halyard Buyers Advocacy: That's sensible. I'll leave all the numbers stuff for Dan. While we wait, can I ask some more about what you want?

63
00:05:38.966 --> 00:05:45.555
Nadia Pearce | Halyard Buyers Advocacy: So, location, you said near Chermside, what suburbs have you looked at, or what suburbs are you thinking?

64
00:05:45.838 --> 00:05:50.340
Tash Kumar: Um, Kedron, Stafford, maybe Nundah? Wavell Heights? I don't know if that's realistic.

65
00:05:51.222 --> 00:05:58.233
Nadia Pearce | Halyard Buyers Advocacy: Wavell Heights houses are well out of reach unfortunately, they're really expensive now, but there are a few townhouses around the edges.

66
00:05:58.233 --> 00:06:04.289
Nadia Pearce | Halyard Buyers Advocacy: Kedron, Stafford, Stafford Heights, Chermside, Chermside West, Nundah, Wooloowin, Gordon Park even, those all have a lot of townhouses.

67
00:06:04.289 --> 00:06:08.751
Nadia Pearce | Halyard Buyers Advocacy: And then houses, maybe Gee bung, Zillmere, Aspley, but it's going to be tight.

68
00:06:09.500 --> 00:06:13.256
Rhys Gallagher: Aspley would be good, it's close to my mum.

69
00:06:13.850 --> 00:06:16.410
Tash Kumar: We're not buying near your mum.

70
00:06:17.386 --> 00:06:18.860
Rhys Gallagher: I'm just saying.

71
00:06:19.871 --> 00:06:23.969
Nadia Pearce | Halyard Buyers Advocacy: Ha. Okay, I'll put Aspley on the list but in pencil.

72
00:06:24.297 --> 00:06:27.114
iPhone (2): Hello? Hi. Sorry. Can you hear me?

73
00:06:27.390 --> 00:06:29.111
Nadia Pearce | Halyard Buyers Advocacy: Hi! Is that Dan?

74
00:06:29.501 --> 00:06:34.780
iPhone (2): Yeah, it's Dan, sorry, I'm on my phone, I'm in the car outside my last appointment.

75
00:06:34.780 --> 00:06:38.738
iPhone (2): I couldn't get the laptop to connect. Can you hear me okay?

76
00:06:39.097 --> 00:06:43.333
Nadia Pearce | Halyard Buyers Advocacy: We can hear you fine. Hi, I'm Nadia, nice to meet you.

77
00:06:44.038 --> 00:06:47.061
iPhone (2): Hi Nadia, nice to meet you. Hi guys.

78
00:06:48.030 --> 00:06:49.088
Tash Kumar: Hi Dan.

79
00:06:49.970 --> 00:06:50.640
Rhys Gallagher: G'day.

80
00:06:51.138 --> 00:06:57.821
Nadia Pearce | Halyard Buyers Advocacy: So we were just talking about budget and I said I'd leave all of the hard stuff for you.

81
00:06:58.437 --> 00:07:03.204
iPhone (2): Ha. Great. Thanks. Um, so, okay. Let me just get my notes up.

82
00:07:03.204 --> 00:07:08.705
iPhone (2): So, I had a first chat with Rhys and Tash a couple of weeks ago,

83
00:07:08.705 --> 00:07:16.772
iPhone (2): and I've had a look at their payslips and a few other bits and pieces, so I've got a reasonably good picture.

84
00:07:16.772 --> 00:07:23.373
iPhone (2): Is it okay if I go through it here, guys? Nadia's going to hear your income and everything.

85
00:07:23.867 --> 00:07:25.379
Tash Kumar: Yeah, it's fine.

86
00:07:26.372 --> 00:07:27.551
Rhys Gallagher: Yeah, all good.

87
00:07:28.161 --> 00:07:32.579
iPhone (2): Okay. So, both of you are full time, permanent, which is great.

88
00:07:32.579 --> 00:07:38.101
iPhone (2): Rhys, your base is around ninety-five and then you do a fair bit of overtime,

89
00:07:38.101 --> 00:07:41.415
iPhone (2): so with that you're about a hundred and ten.

90
00:07:41.415 --> 00:07:48.778
iPhone (2): Tash, you're around eighty-eight base and then with your penalties and night shift allowances, you're around a hundred and five.

91
00:07:48.778 --> 00:07:50.987
iPhone (2): So combined, two-fifteen, give or take.

92
00:07:51.934 --> 00:07:52.479
Nadia Pearce | Halyard Buyers Advocacy: Okay.

93
00:07:52.754 --> 00:07:58.239
iPhone (2): Now, the thing with overtime and penalties is the banks don't always count all of it.

94
00:07:58.239 --> 00:08:03.382
iPhone (2): Most of the lenders I'd use for you will count, like, eighty percent of it,

95
00:08:03.382 --> 00:08:07.496
iPhone (2): if it's been consistent for at least six months, which yours has.

96
00:08:07.496 --> 00:08:11.611
iPhone (2): So for borrowing purposes, I'm working on a bit less than two-fifteen.

97
00:08:12.520 --> 00:08:13.292
Tash Kumar: Okay.

98
00:08:13.805 --> 00:08:20.656
iPhone (2): And then, Tash has a Hex debt, about twenty-eight thousand, and that does affect how much you can borrow,

99
00:08:20.656 --> 00:08:26.786
iPhone (2): because it comes out of your pay. And Rhys has got the car loan on the ute.

100
00:08:27.127 --> 00:08:28.544
Rhys Gallagher: Eighteen left on it.

101
00:08:29.367 --> 00:08:32.909
iPhone (2): Yeah, about eighteen. So that's another repayment the bank counts.

102
00:08:32.909 --> 00:08:38.930
iPhone (2): If there's any way to pay that off, it would actually help your borrowing quite a bit,

103
00:08:38.930 --> 00:08:44.951
iPhone (2): but I wouldn't want you to empty your savings to do it. We can talk about that.

104
00:08:45.924 --> 00:08:48.245
Rhys Gallagher: Yeah, I've been thinking about that.

105
00:08:48.698 --> 00:08:49.079
iPhone (2): Okay.

106
00:08:49.079 --> 00:08:57.458
iPhone (2): So, putting all that together, at the moment I think a lender would approve you for a loan of around nine hundred,

107
00:08:57.458 --> 00:09:03.552
iPhone (2): maybe a little bit more. But I don't want to put you at the absolute max.

108
00:09:03.552 --> 00:09:11.551
iPhone (2): The banks assess you at a rate that's about three percent above what you'd actually pay, so there's already a buffer,

109
00:09:11.551 --> 00:09:16.121
iPhone (2): but still, I'd rather you're comfortable. Especially if, you know, anything changes.

110
00:09:16.811 --> 00:09:23.310
Nadia Pearce | Halyard Buyers Advocacy: Can I ask, Dan, on the five percent deposit scheme, what's the price cap in Brisbane at the moment?

111
00:09:24.351 --> 00:09:26.807
iPhone (2): Yeah, so it's a million in Brisbane.

112
00:09:26.807 --> 00:09:34.177
iPhone (2): Since they changed it in October last year, there's no income caps anymore and no limit on places. So they qualify.

113
00:09:34.177 --> 00:09:40.844
iPhone (2): The way it works is they put in five percent, the government guarantees the rest of the twenty percent,

114
00:09:40.844 --> 00:09:47.160
iPhone (2): and they don't pay lenders mortgage insurance. Which, on a nine hundred thousand purchase, is a big saving.

115
00:09:47.160 --> 00:09:49.266
iPhone (2): Like, thirty, forty grand, sometimes more.

116
00:09:49.659 --> 00:09:50.181
Tash Kumar: Wow.

117
00:09:50.573 --> 00:09:57.106
iPhone (2): So, with eighty-five saved, and say we're buying at, um, let's say nine hundred. Five percent is forty-five.

118
00:09:57.106 --> 00:09:58.921
iPhone (2): Then you've got stamp duty.

119
00:09:59.408 --> 00:10:02.685
Nadia Pearce | Halyard Buyers Advocacy: And that's the bit that hurts on established property.

120
00:10:03.408 --> 00:10:10.970
iPhone (2): Yeah, exactly. So, Nadia knows this, but for you guys, in Queensland, if you're a first home buyer buying an established home,

121
00:10:10.970 --> 00:10:18.188
iPhone (2): you get a full stamp duty concession up to seven hundred thousand, and then it phases out up to eight hundred.

122
00:10:18.188 --> 00:10:25.062
iPhone (2): Above eight hundred, you don't get the first home concession at all, you just get the normal home concession rate.

123
00:10:25.062 --> 00:10:30.561
iPhone (2): So on a nine hundred thousand townhouse, you'd be paying about twenty-six thousand in stamp duty.

124
00:10:31.067 --> 00:10:32.384
Rhys Gallagher: Oh. Shit. Sorry.

125
00:10:32.963 --> 00:10:35.210
iPhone (2): Ha. No, that's the normal reaction.

126
00:10:35.592 --> 00:10:38.529
Tash Kumar: So nine hundred plus forty-five plus twenty-six.

127
00:10:41.336 --> 00:10:49.178
iPhone (2): So forty-five for the deposit, twenty-six-ish for stamp duty, then you've got your legal costs, your building and pest, bank fees,

128
00:10:49.178 --> 00:10:57.020
iPhone (2): a couple of grand in moving. Call it seventy-eight, eighty thousand in total. So you're basically using all of your eighty-five.

129
00:10:57.848 --> 00:11:00.046
Tash Kumar: Okay. That's kind of scary.

130
00:11:00.573 --> 00:11:05.435
iPhone (2): It is a bit tight. That's why I want to talk about it.

131
00:11:05.435 --> 00:11:12.915
iPhone (2): Now, the other side of it, and this is where it gets interesting, if you buy a brand new property,

132
00:11:12.915 --> 00:11:20.395
iPhone (2): so a new build or off the plan, first home buyers in Queensland now pay no stamp duty at all.

133
00:11:20.395 --> 00:11:27.127
iPhone (2): That came in May last year. So on a brand new townhouse, there's twenty-six grand you don't pay.

134
00:11:27.443 --> 00:11:28.562
Rhys Gallagher: Oh, really?

135
00:11:29.424 --> 00:11:34.780
iPhone (2): Yeah. And there's the first home owner grant on new homes as well, which, um,

136
00:11:34.780 --> 00:11:41.564
iPhone (2): I'd need to double check what it is now, it changed at the end of the last financial year,

137
00:11:41.564 --> 00:11:47.277
iPhone (2): I don't want to give you the wrong number. I'll confirm that and send it through.

138
00:11:48.045 --> 00:11:54.331
Nadia Pearce | Halyard Buyers Advocacy: Can I just add one thing on the new build stuff, Dan, just so they've got both sides?

139
00:11:55.330 --> 00:11:56.686
iPhone (2): Yeah, of course.

140
00:11:57.240 --> 00:12:00.834
Nadia Pearce | Halyard Buyers Advocacy: So, new can be great, especially with the duty saving.

141
00:12:00.834 --> 00:12:06.225
Nadia Pearce | Halyard Buyers Advocacy: But new townhouses, especially off the plan, they can be harder on the resale side,

142
00:12:06.225 --> 00:12:11.257
Nadia Pearce | Halyard Buyers Advocacy: because you're competing with the developer who's still selling the rest of the complex.

143
00:12:11.257 --> 00:12:16.649
Nadia Pearce | Halyard Buyers Advocacy: And sometimes the bank valuation on new stuff comes in lower than what you paid,

144
00:12:16.649 --> 00:12:19.883
Nadia Pearce | Halyard Buyers Advocacy: which is a problem with a five percent deposit.

145
00:12:20.837 --> 00:12:25.989
iPhone (2): Yeah, that's a really good point. Valuations on new can be a bit of a risk.

146
00:12:25.989 --> 00:12:31.786
iPhone (2): If the bank values it at less than the contract price, you'd have to make up the difference.

147
00:12:31.786 --> 00:12:35.328
iPhone (2): So I always want the valuation done before you go unconditional.

148
00:12:35.977 --> 00:12:39.464
Nadia Pearce | Halyard Buyers Advocacy: And there's the build quality question, which I'll look at.

149
00:12:39.464 --> 00:12:45.393
Nadia Pearce | Halyard Buyers Advocacy: Some of the new complexes around Chermside and Stafford are great, and some are, um, less great.

150
00:12:45.930 --> 00:12:51.573
Rhys Gallagher: Ha. Yeah. I've done the electrical on some of those. Some of them are, um, yeah.

151
00:12:51.988 --> 00:12:54.576
Nadia Pearce | Halyard Buyers Advocacy: Ha. You'd know better than me!

152
00:12:55.491 --> 00:12:59.832
Tash Kumar: So what's the actual number then? Like what should we be looking at?

153
00:13:00.249 --> 00:13:02.549
iPhone (2): Okay, so here's where I'd land it.

154
00:13:02.549 --> 00:13:09.120
iPhone (2): For an established townhouse or house, I'd want you at about eight-eighty to nine hundred, maybe nine-ten at a stretch.

155
00:13:09.120 --> 00:13:12.405
iPhone (2): That keeps a little bit of your savings left over.

156
00:13:12.405 --> 00:13:18.319
iPhone (2): For a brand new property where you're not paying stamp duty, you could go up to about nine-fifty,

157
00:13:18.319 --> 00:13:20.619
iPhone (2): because you've got that extra twenty-odd thousand.

158
00:13:21.419 --> 00:13:23.157
Nadia Pearce | Halyard Buyers Advocacy: Okay. That's really helpful.

159
00:13:23.409 --> 00:13:30.071
iPhone (2): And look, if Rhys paid off some of the car loan, and if Tash's grandma's gift comes through,

160
00:13:30.071 --> 00:13:31.921
iPhone (2): that changes things a bit.

161
00:13:32.329 --> 00:13:37.947
Tash Kumar: Oh, yeah, that's, um. My nan said she'd give us ten thousand. But I don't know when.

162
00:13:38.526 --> 00:13:45.308
iPhone (2): Yeah, so if that happens, we just need a gift letter from her, saying it's a gift, not a loan.

163
00:13:45.308 --> 00:13:50.056
iPhone (2): It's not hard. But I'm not including it until it's actually in your account.

164
00:13:50.753 --> 00:13:51.428
Tash Kumar: Okay.

165
00:13:51.992 --> 00:13:58.092
Nadia Pearce | Halyard Buyers Advocacy: Dan, what's the timeline on pre-approval? Because I'd want that in place before we're making offers.

166
00:13:58.520 --> 00:14:04.243
iPhone (2): So I can lodge it this week, as long as I get the last few documents.

167
00:14:04.243 --> 00:14:10.682
iPhone (2): Rhys, I still need your last two payslips, the ones from October, and Tash, I need your roster,

168
00:14:10.682 --> 00:14:17.836
iPhone (2): or something from the hospital that shows your penalties are regular. And I need the statement for the car loan.

169
00:14:17.836 --> 00:14:25.348
iPhone (2): Then pre-approval's usually a few days, maybe a week with the lender I'm thinking of. It's normally good for ninety days.

170
00:14:25.616 --> 00:14:28.820
Tash Kumar: I can get the roster thing from my manager.

171
00:14:29.495 --> 00:14:32.035
Rhys Gallagher: I'll send you the payslips tonight.

172
00:14:33.067 --> 00:14:38.537
iPhone (2): Perfect. Then I'll send you guys the documents for the gift letter too, just in case.

173
00:14:38.851 --> 00:14:43.751
Nadia Pearce | Halyard Buyers Advocacy: Thanks Dan. This is really clear. Anything else on your side, before you go?

174
00:14:44.579 --> 00:14:49.569
iPhone (2): Um, just one thing. Rates. You know, the rate you get matters a lot.

175
00:14:49.569 --> 00:14:56.698
iPhone (2): On the five percent scheme, not every lender has the best rates, so I'll show you a couple of options.

176
00:14:56.698 --> 00:15:03.470
iPhone (2): And the other thing, when you guys get a property under contract, tell me straight away, on the day,

177
00:15:03.470 --> 00:15:09.529
iPhone (2): because I'll need to order the valuation, and the finance clause is usually fourteen or twenty-one days,

178
00:15:09.529 --> 00:15:11.668
iPhone (2): and the banks can be slow.

179
00:15:12.572 --> 00:15:19.345
Nadia Pearce | Halyard Buyers Advocacy: Yeah, I always try for twenty-one on finance for first home buyers. We don't always get it, but I try.

180
00:15:19.867 --> 00:15:25.330
iPhone (2): Great. Okay, guys, I've got to run, I've got another client in Albion at four thirty.

181
00:15:25.330 --> 00:15:27.721
iPhone (2): But I'll send everything through tonight, okay?

182
00:15:28.217 --> 00:15:29.895
Tash Kumar: Thanks so much Dan.

183
00:15:30.667 --> 00:15:31.855
Rhys Gallagher: Cheers mate.

184
00:15:32.862 --> 00:15:36.653
Nadia Pearce | Halyard Buyers Advocacy: Thanks Dan, great to meet you, I'll email you after this.

185
00:15:37.079 --> 00:15:38.751
iPhone (2): Thanks Nadia. Bye guys.

186
00:15:39.658 --> 00:15:42.056
Tash Kumar: Okay. Wow. That was a lot.

187
00:15:42.772 --> 00:15:46.179
Nadia Pearce | Halyard Buyers Advocacy: It was a lot. How are you feeling?

188
00:15:47.085 --> 00:15:50.987
Tash Kumar: Um. Honestly, like, a bit overwhelmed? But also, it's good to know.

189
00:15:50.987 --> 00:15:56.839
Tash Kumar: Like, we always thought it'd be nine-fifty, and it's sort of, it's less than that, unless it's new.

190
00:15:57.411 --> 00:16:02.748
Rhys Gallagher: But nine hundred's still good. Like, that townhouse in Kedron would've been in range.

191
00:16:04.720 --> 00:16:08.911
Nadia Pearce | Halyard Buyers Advocacy: Yeah, nine hundred is genuinely a good budget for what you want.

192
00:16:08.911 --> 00:16:14.499
Nadia Pearce | Halyard Buyers Advocacy: Let me tell you what I think that buys, and then how I'd work with you.

193
00:16:14.499 --> 00:16:21.485
Nadia Pearce | Halyard Buyers Advocacy: So in Kedron, Stafford, Chermside, at eight-eighty to nine hundred, you're looking at a three bed townhouse, probably two bathrooms,

194
00:16:21.485 --> 00:16:29.169
Nadia Pearce | Halyard Buyers Advocacy: double lock up garage or a single plus a car space, in a complex of somewhere between, like, six and thirty townhouses.

195
00:16:29.169 --> 00:16:36.504
Nadia Pearce | Halyard Buyers Advocacy: Older ones, from the two thousands, are often a bit bigger, with bigger courtyards. Newer ones are smaller but more modern.

196
00:16:36.504 --> 00:16:40.346
Nadia Pearce | Halyard Buyers Advocacy: In Nundah and Wooloowin, it's similar but a bit more competition.

197
00:16:40.346 --> 00:16:45.585
Nadia Pearce | Halyard Buyers Advocacy: And a house, at nine hundred, I'd be honest, it's very hard in those suburbs.

198
00:16:45.585 --> 00:16:51.872
Nadia Pearce | Halyard Buyers Advocacy: Geebung and Zillmere you might get something small, older, on a small block, but it would need work,

199
00:16:51.872 --> 00:16:54.317
Nadia Pearce | Halyard Buyers Advocacy: and it's not near the train necessarily.

200
00:16:55.270 --> 00:16:57.761
Tash Kumar: I don't need near the train.

201
00:16:58.630 --> 00:17:01.561
Nadia Pearce | Halyard Buyers Advocacy: No, you need near work. Which is fine.

202
00:17:01.561 --> 00:17:09.620
Nadia Pearce | Halyard Buyers Advocacy: Chermside is actually really good, it's close to the shopping centre, close to the hospital. And then there's the double garage thing.

203
00:17:09.620 --> 00:17:16.214
Nadia Pearce | Halyard Buyers Advocacy: Rhys, would a single lock up plus a car space work, or do you really need a double?

204
00:17:16.478 --> 00:17:23.806
Rhys Gallagher: Single lock up is fine as long as I can lock the tools in it. Tash's car can go out the front.

205
00:17:24.766 --> 00:17:27.620
Tash Kumar: My car's a Yaris. Nobody's stealing it.

206
00:17:27.976 --> 00:17:32.014
Nadia Pearce | Halyard Buyers Advocacy: Ha. Okay. And then body corporate, so I'd be looking at the levies.

207
00:17:32.014 --> 00:17:38.848
Nadia Pearce | Halyard Buyers Advocacy: On a townhouse, they could be anything from like two and a half thousand a year to six or seven thousand a

208
00:17:38.848 --> 00:17:45.371
Nadia Pearce | Halyard Buyers Advocacy: year, depending on what's in the complex. Pool, gardens, lifts. And the sinking fund, which is the savings for big repairs.

209
00:17:45.371 --> 00:17:50.031
Nadia Pearce | Halyard Buyers Advocacy: If the sinking fund is low, that's often a sign there's a big bill coming.

210
00:17:50.031 --> 00:17:54.690
Nadia Pearce | Halyard Buyers Advocacy: I always read the body corporate records, the minutes, the disputes. Those are really important.

211
00:17:55.559 --> 00:17:58.946
Tash Kumar: I wouldn't even know what to look for.

212
00:17:59.820 --> 00:18:04.897
Nadia Pearce | Halyard Buyers Advocacy: That's what I do. Honestly, for townhouses, the body corporate stuff is about half the work.

213
00:18:04.897 --> 00:18:11.878
Nadia Pearce | Halyard Buyers Advocacy: The other half is the building itself. Like, is there water coming in, is there cracking, has there been a defect claim.

214
00:18:11.878 --> 00:18:16.003
Nadia Pearce | Halyard Buyers Advocacy: Some of the newer complexes around here have had big issues with waterproofing.

215
00:18:18.813 --> 00:18:20.566
Rhys Gallagher: Yeah, we see that.

216
00:18:20.880 --> 00:18:25.171
Nadia Pearce | Halyard Buyers Advocacy: Okay, so, the other question is, what do you want me to do?

217
00:18:25.171 --> 00:18:32.433
Nadia Pearce | Halyard Buyers Advocacy: Because I can do the whole thing, which is the full search, or there's a couple of smaller options that a lot

218
00:18:32.433 --> 00:18:34.084
Nadia Pearce | Halyard Buyers Advocacy: of first home buyers use.

219
00:18:34.472 --> 00:18:36.165
Tash Kumar: What are the options?

220
00:18:37.206 --> 00:18:40.692
Nadia Pearce | Halyard Buyers Advocacy: So, the full service is what most people do.

221
00:18:40.692 --> 00:18:46.114
Nadia Pearce | Halyard Buyers Advocacy: We start with a brief session, then I search, on market and off market.

222
00:18:46.114 --> 00:18:54.635
Nadia Pearce | Halyard Buyers Advocacy: A lot of townhouses that sell before they hit the portals, a selling agent will call me because they know I've got

223
00:18:54.635 --> 00:18:55.797
Nadia Pearce | Halyard Buyers Advocacy: a buyer ready.

224
00:18:55.797 --> 00:19:03.543
Nadia Pearce | Halyard Buyers Advocacy: I'd inspect for you, do all the due diligence, the body corporate, the building, the comparable sales, and then negotiate,

225
00:19:03.543 --> 00:19:08.965
Nadia Pearce | Halyard Buyers Advocacy: or bid at auction, and then I look after it right through to settlement.

226
00:19:08.965 --> 00:19:15.162
Nadia Pearce | Halyard Buyers Advocacy: The fee for that is an engagement fee of two and a half thousand plus GST,

227
00:19:15.162 --> 00:19:23.683
Nadia Pearce | Halyard Buyers Advocacy: and then one point eight percent of the price plus GST when you buy. With a minimum of fifteen thousand plus GST.

228
00:19:23.683 --> 00:19:27.169
Nadia Pearce | Halyard Buyers Advocacy: And the engagement fee comes off at the end.

229
00:19:27.529 --> 00:19:30.031
Rhys Gallagher: So at nine hundred, that's, um—

230
00:19:30.263 --> 00:19:32.343
Nadia Pearce | Halyard Buyers Advocacy: Sixteen thousand two hundred plus GST.

231
00:19:32.644 --> 00:19:36.167
Rhys Gallagher: Yeah. That's, um. That's a lot, for us, honestly.

232
00:19:36.771 --> 00:19:40.052
Nadia Pearce | Halyard Buyers Advocacy: No, I totally understand, and I'd rather you were honest.

233
00:19:40.052 --> 00:19:45.629
Nadia Pearce | Halyard Buyers Advocacy: So the other options are, we've got a negotiate only service, where you find the property yourself,

234
00:19:45.629 --> 00:19:51.862
Nadia Pearce | Halyard Buyers Advocacy: and you bring it to me, and I do the due diligence, I look at the body corporate records,

235
00:19:51.862 --> 00:19:57.112
Nadia Pearce | Halyard Buyers Advocacy: I tell you what it's worth, and I negotiate it for you, or bid at auction.

236
00:19:57.112 --> 00:20:00.064
Nadia Pearce | Halyard Buyers Advocacy: That one's five and a half thousand plus GST.

237
00:20:00.064 --> 00:20:06.298
Nadia Pearce | Halyard Buyers Advocacy: And then there's just auction bidding, where I just bid on the day, and that's fifteen hundred plus GST.

238
00:20:06.945 --> 00:20:09.094
Tash Kumar: Oh, okay. That's, um, that's interesting.

239
00:20:09.714 --> 00:20:13.792
Rhys Gallagher: The negotiate one would be good. Because we can look ourselves.

240
00:20:14.339 --> 00:20:18.549
Tash Kumar: But then we have to do all the looking. With my shifts.

241
00:20:19.248 --> 00:20:20.068
Rhys Gallagher: Yeah. True.

242
00:20:21.036 --> 00:20:24.130
Nadia Pearce | Halyard Buyers Advocacy: Honestly, I'd say have a think about it.

243
00:20:24.130 --> 00:20:29.931
Nadia Pearce | Halyard Buyers Advocacy: The thing with the full service is mostly the off market stuff and the time.

244
00:20:29.931 --> 00:20:33.024
Nadia Pearce | Halyard Buyers Advocacy: With your shifts, Tash, that's a real thing.

245
00:20:33.024 --> 00:20:39.599
Nadia Pearce | Halyard Buyers Advocacy: But if you're happy to keep looking on the weekends, the negotiate one is really good value,

246
00:20:39.599 --> 00:20:42.692
Nadia Pearce | Halyard Buyers Advocacy: a lot of first home buyers use that.

247
00:20:43.214 --> 00:20:46.358
Tash Kumar: Okay. Can you send us both? Like, the details?

248
00:20:47.341 --> 00:20:48.076
Nadia Pearce | Halyard Buyers Advocacy: Of course.

249
00:20:48.076 --> 00:20:56.170
Nadia Pearce | Halyard Buyers Advocacy: And just so you know, whichever one you pick, we can't do anything until you sign the agreement, it's a Form 6,

250
00:20:56.170 --> 00:21:00.216
Nadia Pearce | Halyard Buyers Advocacy: it's the Queensland form, so I'll attach that for both options.

251
00:21:01.153 --> 00:21:01.701
Rhys Gallagher: Okay.

252
00:21:02.507 --> 00:21:10.520
Nadia Pearce | Halyard Buyers Advocacy: Can I ask a couple more things before we finish? Just for my notes. Are you okay with an older complex?

253
00:21:10.520 --> 00:21:12.809
Nadia Pearce | Halyard Buyers Advocacy: Like, from the eighties or nineties?

254
00:21:13.317 --> 00:21:16.452
Tash Kumar: Um. As long as it's, like, not gross.

255
00:21:16.838 --> 00:21:19.635
Rhys Gallagher: As long as the wiring's not stuffed.

256
00:21:20.679 --> 00:21:27.664
Nadia Pearce | Halyard Buyers Advocacy: Ha. You'd be the one to check that. Okay, and are there any things you definitely don't want?

257
00:21:27.664 --> 00:21:30.768
Nadia Pearce | Halyard Buyers Advocacy: Like, main roads, flood, that kind of thing?

258
00:21:31.637 --> 00:21:36.632
Tash Kumar: Not on Gympie Road. I don't want to be on Gympie Road.

259
00:21:37.384 --> 00:21:38.762
Rhys Gallagher: Or Webster Road.

260
00:21:39.047 --> 00:21:43.845
Nadia Pearce | Halyard Buyers Advocacy: Okay. Main roads, no. What about the train line, or the busway, or flight paths?

261
00:21:43.845 --> 00:21:48.323
Nadia Pearce | Halyard Buyers Advocacy: Some of the parts of Nundah and Kedron get a bit of plane noise.

262
00:21:49.202 --> 00:21:55.024
Tash Kumar: Oh, I didn't think about planes. I sleep during the day sometimes. That would be bad.

263
00:21:55.755 --> 00:22:00.778
Nadia Pearce | Halyard Buyers Advocacy: Yeah, so that's a good one, with your nights. I'll check the flight paths.

264
00:22:00.778 --> 00:22:06.159
Nadia Pearce | Halyard Buyers Advocacy: And noise generally, because some townhouses share walls and if your neighbour's got a toddler,

265
00:22:06.159 --> 00:22:09.747
Nadia Pearce | Halyard Buyers Advocacy: and you're trying to sleep at eleven in the morning.

266
00:22:10.761 --> 00:22:13.658
Tash Kumar: Oh God. Yeah. Like, end unit would be good.

267
00:22:13.658 --> 00:22:18.166
Tash Kumar: Or at least not, um, like, the bedroom not next to someone else's bedroom.

268
00:22:18.891 --> 00:22:22.483
Nadia Pearce | Halyard Buyers Advocacy: Yep. That's a really good one, I'll put that on.

269
00:22:22.483 --> 00:22:27.872
Nadia Pearce | Halyard Buyers Advocacy: And flooding, Kedron Brook runs through a few of those suburbs, so I always check.

270
00:22:28.344 --> 00:22:29.339
Rhys Gallagher: No flooding.

271
00:22:29.785 --> 00:22:33.670
Nadia Pearce | Halyard Buyers Advocacy: No flooding. Okay. And timing, is there a lease ending?

272
00:22:34.293 --> 00:22:40.624
Tash Kumar: Our lease is up in April. And we don't want to renew it, honestly, with the rent.

273
00:22:41.494 --> 00:22:45.721
Nadia Pearce | Halyard Buyers Advocacy: Okay, so April gives us a bit of time. That's good.

274
00:22:45.721 --> 00:22:50.332
Nadia Pearce | Halyard Buyers Advocacy: What we don't want is to rush and buy the wrong thing.

275
00:22:50.332 --> 00:22:58.786
Nadia Pearce | Halyard Buyers Advocacy: Dan said ninety days for pre-approval, so if he lodges this week, that takes us to about February. That's a good window.

276
00:22:59.196 --> 00:22:59.999
Tash Kumar: Okay.

277
00:23:00.545 --> 00:23:03.187
Rhys Gallagher: Do we have to buy before Christmas?

278
00:23:03.685 --> 00:23:09.541
Nadia Pearce | Halyard Buyers Advocacy: No. Absolutely not. There's usually a quieter period over Christmas, and then February, March gets busy again.

279
00:23:09.541 --> 00:23:16.776
Nadia Pearce | Halyard Buyers Advocacy: You might find something before Christmas, sometimes the best deals are in December when there's less people looking. But no pressure.

280
00:23:17.597 --> 00:23:18.884
Tash Kumar: Okay. That's good.

281
00:23:19.778 --> 00:23:20.771
Nadia Pearce | Halyard Buyers Advocacy: So, next steps.

282
00:23:20.771 --> 00:23:27.393
Nadia Pearce | Halyard Buyers Advocacy: I'll send you an email tonight, with the summary of what we talked about, both service options, and the agreement.

283
00:23:27.393 --> 00:23:33.684
Nadia Pearce | Halyard Buyers Advocacy: Dan's going to send you his document list. You're going to send him the payslips and the roster thing.

284
00:23:34.698 --> 00:23:35.518
Rhys Gallagher: Payslips tonight.

285
00:23:36.483 --> 00:23:40.358
Tash Kumar: I'll ask my manager tomorrow night when I'm on.

286
00:23:40.795 --> 00:23:45.866
Nadia Pearce | Halyard Buyers Advocacy: Perfect. And then have a think about which service you want, no rush.

287
00:23:45.866 --> 00:23:54.057
Nadia Pearce | Halyard Buyers Advocacy: If you want, I'm happy to look at a couple of listings for you this weekend, even before you sign anything,

288
00:23:54.057 --> 00:23:57.567
Nadia Pearce | Halyard Buyers Advocacy: and just tell you what I think. Just informally.

289
00:23:58.189 --> 00:24:00.034
Tash Kumar: Oh, that would be amazing.

290
00:24:01.013 --> 00:24:07.147
Nadia Pearce | Halyard Buyers Advocacy: Send me links. Anything you're thinking of going to, send it through, and I'll give you my two cents.

291
00:24:07.940 --> 00:24:12.333
Rhys Gallagher: There's one in Stafford we were going to look at on Saturday.

292
00:24:12.652 --> 00:24:14.181
Nadia Pearce | Halyard Buyers Advocacy: Send it. Okay?

293
00:24:15.091 --> 00:24:16.104
Rhys Gallagher: Will do.

294
00:24:17.143 --> 00:24:20.709
Nadia Pearce | Halyard Buyers Advocacy: Great. Thank you both. And Tash, go have a nap.

295
00:24:21.112 --> 00:24:24.436
Tash Kumar: Ha. I'm going to. Thank you so much, Nadia.

296
00:24:25.368 --> 00:24:26.178
Rhys Gallagher: Thanks, Nadia.

297
00:24:27.012 --> 00:24:27.814
Nadia Pearce | Halyard Buyers Advocacy: Bye!
